\title{TPU memory hierarchy}
\taxon{Definition}
\tag{public}
\p{The TPU memory hierarchy is entirely software managed with no cache. Memory movement is controlled by the compiler and [[PMIC]].}
\figure{
\<html:img>[width]{60\%}[src]{\route-asset{assets/img/tpu-mem-hierarchy.png}}{}
\figcaption{Datapath through a TPU onto the execution unit [[OGCRP]] or [[OGCRN]].}
}
\p{Notably, in [[060Z]], you tile the memory transfer and define the pipeline from HBM to VMEM.}
